  "description": "How do animals stay cool on a hot day? Pick your answer with Milo the bluebird, then find out: an elephant flaps its big ears and sprays water and mud on its wrinkly skin, a koala stretches out its arms and legs when it is hot and folds them in when it is cold, and a big tiger cools off by lying in a shady pool.\nAn interactive animal lesson for kids ages 2-6, with questions to answer, actions to copy, quick checks and a quiz at the end.\n\nThe Animated Zoo makes gentle, colorful videos for little learners. New videos every day! Made with care for ages 2-6. Characters and visuals are animated with the help of AI tools and reviewed for kid safety before publishing.",
